## Documentation layout

- **`.agents/` is how we work** (the harness); **`docs/` is what we build** (the product).
- Approved plans go in `docs/plans/<yyyy-mm>-<slug>.md`. Set the plan's `**Status:**` line to `Shipped (#PR)` when it merges.
- `docs/next-steps.md` is the session handoff: overwrite it at the end of each slice.
- **Living docs vs records.** Living docs (`AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, `docs/next-steps.md`) must match the present. Records (shipped plans, `.agents/memory/*`) are never rewritten; the only allowed edits are status lines and link paths after a move.
- Move files with `git mv`, in a commit with no content edits, so history follows the file.

## How we work: the plan, review, implement, review loop

For any change larger than a typo or a one-line config tweak:

1. **Plan first.** Run the `planner` persona (or `.agents/workflows/plan.md`) with a one-line goal. It returns a numbered plan with file paths and acceptance criteria. No code yet.
2. **{{OWNER}} reviews the plan.** Approves, edits, or rejects.
<!-- kit:if has.checks -->
3. **Implement.** Implement the approved plan step by step. Run `{{CMD_CHECKS}}` before declaring done. A check that can't run is reported "not run: <reason>", never "passed".
<!-- kit:end -->
<!-- kit:if !has.checks -->
3. **Implement.** Implement the approved plan step by step. The project has no typecheck, lint or test command yet: report each check as "not run: no command".
<!-- kit:end -->
<!-- kit:if has.container -->
   If the diff touches the container image or boot path (`.agents/rules/production-parity.md`), a container run is the evidence. A host build is never evidence that production works.
<!-- kit:end -->
4. **Review the diff.** Run the `reviewer` persona (or `.agents/workflows/review.md`). Independent context, fresh read. The reviewer audits against conventions and drift checks, and may approve or request changes.
5. **{{OWNER}} validates** the change where it runs, when relevant.
<!-- kit:if module.openPr -->
6. **Always ask {{OWNER}} before merging to `main`.** When {{OWNER}} asks for a PR, open it with `open-pr`. Never merge a branch or PR autonomously. Present the diff summary and green checks, and ask for explicit approval.
<!-- kit:end -->
<!-- kit:if !module.openPr -->
6. **Always ask {{OWNER}} before merging to `main`.** Never merge a branch or PR autonomously. Present the diff summary and green checks, and ask for explicit approval.
<!-- kit:end -->
7. **Memorialize.** At session end, follow `.agents/workflows/retro.md`: brief the `retro` persona, which appends to `.agents/memory/lessons.md` and refreshes `docs/next-steps.md`; decisions it flags go to the `architect` as proposed ADRs.

The reviewer pass is non-negotiable. It is the cheapest insurance against confidently wrong code.

## Git & PRs

GitHub flow: `main` is production, and every change reaches it through a PR.

<!-- kit:adapt: Say in one sentence how main reaches production (which host or workflow deploys it, and after which checks). If nothing deploys automatically, say so. -->

- **The main checkout stays on `main`; branch work happens in a worktree.** Claude Code worktree sessions load agents, hooks and settings from the main checkout, so a feature branch left checked out there hands every new session stale harness files. Start each task in a worktree off an up-to-date `main`, and never switch the main checkout's branch.
- **Pull `main` at session start**: fast-forward the main checkout (`git -C <main checkout> pull --ff-only`) before branching.
- Branch from `main` as `{{BRANCH_PREFIX}}/<type>-<slug>`: a Conventional Commit type plus 2 to 5 kebab-case words. Stacked PRs target the branch below; restack when it changes and retarget to `main` once it merges. After the branch below is squash-merged, `git fetch` and restack with `git rebase --onto origin/main <old base SHA>`, where the old base SHA is the last commit of the branch below before the squash.
- Commits and PR titles are Conventional Commits. The PR title becomes the squash commit.
<!-- kit:if module.openPr -->
- Open PRs with the `open-pr` skill: sections in `.github/pull_request_template.md` order, a `Rollback:` line in Notes when a risky path changes, no em dashes, no "Generated with Claude Code" footer and no co-author line.
<!-- kit:end -->
- Squash merge and delete the branch, only with green checks and {{OWNER}}'s explicit approval.
<!-- kit:if module.prePush -->
- Never push to `main`. `.githooks/pre-push` refuses it once you run `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` (one time per clone; worktrees share it). Only {{OWNER}} uses the `{{ENV_PREFIX}}_ALLOW_PUSH_MAIN=1` override. Never use `--no-verify`.
<!-- kit:end -->
<!-- kit:if !module.prePush -->
- Never push to `main`.
<!-- kit:end -->
- Force-push only your own branch, and only with `--force-with-lease`.

