## The team (`.agents/personas/`)

IDs are role-based and are what files, hooks and workflows reference; names are what we call them. Personas run as sub-agents with a fresh context, so brief them fully; their final message is all the caller gets.

| ID | Name | Job | Can | Model |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| (main session) | **{{PERSONA_NAME_BUILDER}}** | Builder: implements approved plans, orchestrates the others, talks with {{OWNER}} | Everything the session allows | session model |
<!-- kit:if has.db -->
| `architect` | **{{PERSONA_NAME_ARCHITECT}}** | Shape of the system: decisions and ADRs, schema and migrations, architecture assessments | Edit `{{DB_PATH}}` and `decisions.md`; local DB Bash | Opus |
<!-- kit:end -->
<!-- kit:if !has.db -->
| `architect` | **{{PERSONA_NAME_ARCHITECT}}** | Shape of the system: decisions and ADRs, architecture assessments | Edit `decisions.md` | Opus |
<!-- kit:end -->
| `planner` | **{{PERSONA_NAME_PLANNER}}** | Step-by-step implementation plans | Read only | Opus |
| `reviewer` | **{{PERSONA_NAME_REVIEWER}}** | Reviews every diff before merge | Read only + git and check Bash | Opus |
| `retro` | **{{PERSONA_NAME_RETRO}}** | End-of-session lesson and handoff | Edit `lessons.md` and `next-steps.md` | Sonnet |
| `researcher` | **{{PERSONA_NAME_RESEARCHER}}** | Researches a topic in its official docs and returns verified facts with URLs | Read only + web search and fetch | Sonnet |

Cost controls: in their Claude wrappers the planner, reviewer and architect run at `effort: medium`, every Opus persona has a `maxTurns` cap, and `.agents/workflows/review.md` sizes each review to the risk of the diff. Raise a persona's effort for a single hard run through the Agent call, not by editing the wrapper.

When to run each:

- **`architect`** (`.agents/personas/architect.md`): architectural decisions and ADRs (boundaries, auth, deploy topology, environment design, new dependencies); architectural assessment of a plan or area. Run it before the planner when a change needs a decision no accepted ADR covers.
<!-- kit:if has.db -->
  It also owns every schema change under `{{DB_PATH}}` (migration, seed update, rollback note).
<!-- kit:end -->
- **`planner`** (`.agents/personas/planner.md`): any change involving more than one file, or any new feature. Always before code.
- **`reviewer`** (`.agents/personas/reviewer.md`): any diff before merging, even self-PRs.
- **`retro`** (`.agents/personas/retro.md`): at end of session or slice, given a brief of what happened. Flags decisions for the `architect` to record as ADRs.
- **`researcher`** (`.agents/personas/researcher.md`): before adopting a dependency or relying on an external tool's behavior. Brief it with the topic, the versions this repo pins, and the questions to answer; it returns facts with official-doc URLs.

